      "title": "India backs every meaningful peace effort in Ukraine, West Asia: PM Modi",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/india-backs-every-meaningful-peace-effort-in-ukraine-west-asia-pm-modi-126102200582_1.html",
      "description": "India will continue to support every meaningful effort to bring peace to Ukraine and West Asia, Prime Minister Narendra Modi said on Thursday after holding wide-ranging talks with his Polish counterpart Donald Tusk.\nTusk is on a three-day visit to India amid renewed global push to end the conflict in Ukraine.\nIn his media statement following the talks, Modi said several decisions were taken to expand the strategic partnership between India and Poland and that both sides are determined to ramp up the overall engagement.\n\"We have reached understanding to deepen relations in defence, space, and nuclear energy. We invite companies from Poland to engage in co-development and co-production with India in all these strategic sectors,\" Modi said.\nThe prime minister said the growing bilateral economic strength has created new opportunities for the India-Poland partnership, adding New Delhi's free trade agreement with the European Union will further solidify the economic engagement between th",
